{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Despite our laws being so weak that they have not been broken, these donations are an insult to voters and gambling reform advocates. Both the major parties accept huge sums of money from big industries, and their policies show it. Weak donation laws mean a $10,000 donation from Sportsbet to the shadow minister responsible for online betting doesn\u8217 t have to be disclosed. More than a third of all donations to parties stay hidden from public view. Sportsbet also spent nearly $9,000 for a campaign dinner and access to the shadow minister \u8211  no requirement to disclose that one either. These donations are not made because Sportsbet loves democracy, they are made for access and to influence policy.}
